Here is the commit message:
bugfix: retargeting logic error

Here is the root cause:
The `retargetTrack` method required a non-null `sourceTrack` (enforced via `Validate.nonNull`), so the calling loop in the retargeting logic had to skip invoking it whenever a target bone had no corresponding source track (i.e., `sourceTrack == null`). This caused the code to `continue` without calling `result.addTrack(track)` for that bone, meaning no track was added at all for target bones lacking a mapped source track. As a result, those bones were left without any animation track in the retargeted animation, instead of being assigned a default/bind-pose track. This is a logic error because every mapped target bone should receive a track in the output animation—even if it just represents the bind pose—rather than being silently skipped.

Here is the patch:
